  "title": "git hooks: Don't warn about empty commit messages",
  "description": "Avoid warning messages about a commit message not following our standards\nif it's empty. Unless a command line flag is given, git will give its\nown warning \"Aborting commit due to empty commit message\" and gracefully\nabort.\n\nPutting in an empty commit message is the way to intentionally abort a\ncommit under certain workflows, e.g. using vim in Linux.\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
